{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-pro-29-1","title":"Proverbs 29:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Observations of public government, 15 and of private. 22 Of anger, pride, thievery, cowardice, and corruption.</p>\n<p>He, that being often reproved. Heb. a man of reproofs. 1:24-31; 1Sa 2:25,34; 1Ki 17:1; 18:18; 20:42; 21:20-23 1Ki 22:20-23,28,34-37; 2Ch 25:16; 33:10; 36:15-17; Jer 25:3-5 Jer 26:3-5; 35:13-16; Zec 1:3-6; Mt 26:21-25; Joh 6:70,71 Joh 13:10,11,18,26; Ac 1:18,25 hardeneth. 2Ch 36:13; Ne 9:29; Isa 48:4; Jer 17:23 shall. 6:15; 28:18; Isa 30:13,14; Zec 7:11-14; 1Th 5:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-2","title":"Proverbs 29:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the righteous. 11:10; 28:12,28; Es 8:15; Ps 72:1-7; Isa 32:1,2; Jer 23:5,6 Re 11:15 in authority. or, increased. when the wicked. Es 3:15; Ec 10:5; Mt 2:3,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-3","title":"Proverbs 29:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>loveth. 10:1; 15:20; 23:15,24,25; 27:11; Lu 1:13-17 he. 5:8-10; 6:26; 21:17,20; 28:7,19; Lu 15:13,30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-4","title":"Proverbs 29:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>king. 14; 16:12; 20:8; 1Sa 13:13; 2Sa 8:15; 1Ki 2:12; Ps 89:14; 99:4 Isa 9:7; 49:8 he that receiveth gifts. Heb. a man of oblations. 2Ki 15:18-20; Jer 22:13-17; Da 11:20; Mic 7:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-5","title":"Proverbs 29:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>that. 7:5,21; 20:19; 26:24,25,28; 2Sa 14:17-24; Job 17:5; Ps 5:9; 12:2 1Th 2:5 spreadeth. 1:17; La 1:13; Ho 5:1; Lu 20:20,21; Ro 16:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-6","title":"Proverbs 29:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>the transgression. 5:22; 11:5,6; 12:13; Job 18:7-10; Ps 11:6; Isa 8:14,15; 2Ti 2:26 but. Ps 97:11; 118:15; 132:16; Ro 5:2,3; Jas 1:2; 1Pe 1:8; 1Jo 1:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-7","title":"Proverbs 29:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>considereth. Job 29:16; 31:13,21; Ps 31:7; 41:1; Ga 6:1 but. 21:13; 1Sa 25:9-11; Jer 5:28; 22:15-17; Eze 22:7,29-31; Mic 3:1-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-8","title":"Proverbs 29:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Scornful. 11:11; Isa 28:14-22; Mt 27:39-43; Joh 9:40,41; 11:47-50 1Th 2:15,16 bring a city into a snare. or, set a city on fire. Jas 3:5,6 wise. Ex 32:10-14; Nu 16:48; 25:11; De 9:18-20; 2Sa 24:16,17; Jer 15:1 Eze 22:30; Am 7:2-6; Jas 5:15-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-9","title":"Proverbs 29:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>26:4; Ec 10:13; Mt 7:6; 11:17-19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-10","title":"Proverbs 29:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>The blood-thirsty. Heb. Men of bloods. Ge 4:5-8; 1Sa 20:31-33; 22:11-23; 1Ki 21:20; 22:8; 2Ch 18:7 Mr 6:18,19,24-27; Joh 15:18,19; 1Jo 3:12,13 but. 1Sa 15:11; Jer 13:15-17; 18:20; 40:14-16; Lu 23:34; Joh 5:34 Ac 7:60; Ro 10:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-11","title":"Proverbs 29:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>12:16,23; 14:33; Jud 16:17; Am 5:13; Mic 7:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-12","title":"Proverbs 29:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>20:8; 25:23; 1Sa 22:8-23; 23:19-23; 2Sa 3:7-11; 4:5-12 1Ki 21:11-13; 2Ki 10:6,7; Ps 52:2-4; 101:5-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-13","title":"Proverbs 29:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>the deceitful man. or, the usurer. Mt 9:9; 1Co 6:10 meet. 22:2; Ex 22:25,26; Le 25:35-37; Ne 5:5-7 Lord. Ps 13:3; Mt 5:45; Eph 2:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-14","title":"Proverbs 29:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>king. 4; 16:12; 20:28; 25:5; 28:16; Job 29:11-18; Ps 72:2-4,12-14; 82:2,3 Ps 89:2; Isa 1:17; 11:4; Jer 5:28; 22:16; Da 4:27 his throne. Isa 9:6,7; Lu 1:32,33; Heb 1:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-15","title":"Proverbs 29:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>a rod. 17,21; 22:6,15; 23:13,14; Heb 12:10,11 a child. 10:1,5; 17:21,25; 1Ki 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-16","title":"Proverbs 29:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the wicked. 2; *marg: but. Ps 37:34,36; 58:10; 91:8; 92:9,11; 112:8; Re 15:4; 18:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-17","title":"Proverbs 29:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>15; 13:24; 19:18; 22:15; 23:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-18","title":"Proverbs 29:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>there. 1Sa 3:1; Ho 4:6; Am 8:11,12; Mt 9:36; Ro 10:13-15 perish. or, is made naked. 2Ch 28:19 but. 19:16; Ps 19:11; 119:2; Lu 11:28; Joh 13:17; 14:21-23; Jas 1:25 Re 22:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-19","title":"Proverbs 29:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>servant. 26:3; 30:22 though. Job 19:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-20","title":"Proverbs 29:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Seest. 11; Ec 5:2; Jas 1:19 words. or, matters. 14:29; 21:5 more. 26:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-22","title":"Proverbs 29:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>angry. 10:12; 15:18; 17:19; 26:21; 30:33 a furious. 17:19; 22:24; Jas 3:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-23","title":"Proverbs 29:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>man's. 18:12; 2Ch 32:25,26; 33:10-12,23,24; Job 22:29; 40:12; Isa 2:11,12 Da 4:30-37; 5:20,21; Lu 14:11; 18:14; Ac 12:23; Jas 4:6-10 1Pe 5:5 honour. 15:33; De 8:2,3,16; Isa 57:15; 66:2; Mt 5:3; 18:4; 23:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-24","title":"Proverbs 29:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>partner. 1:11-19; Ps 50:18-22; Isa 1:23; Mr 11:17 hateth. 6:32; 8:36; 15:32; 20:2 he. Le 5:1; Jud 17:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-25","title":"Proverbs 29:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>fear. Ge 12:11-13; 20:2,11; 26:7; Ex 32:22-24; 1Sa 15:24; 27:1,11 1Ki 19:3; Isa 57:11; Mt 10:28; 15:12; 26:69-74; Joh 3:2; 9:22; 12:42 Joh 19:12,13; Ga 2:11-13; 2Ti 4:16,17 whoso. 16:20; 18:10; 30:5; 1Ch 5:20; Ps 118:8; 125:1; Ec 7:18; Da 3:28; 6:23 1Pe 1:21 safe. Heb. set on high. Ps 69:29; 91:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-26","title":"Proverbs 29:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>seek. 19:6; Ps 20:9 ruler's favour. Heb. face of a ruler. 16:7; 19:21; 21:1; Ge 43:14; Ezr 7:27,28; Ne 1:11; Es 4:16; Ps 20:9 Ps 62:12; Isa 46:9-11; Da 4:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-29-27","title":"Proverbs 29:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>24:9; Ps 119:115; 139:21; Zec 11:8; Joh 7:7; 15:17-19,23 1Jo 3:13</p>"}]}